ELSE - SELECT THE OTHER IF BRANCH

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
ELSE - SELECT THE OTHER IF BRANCH

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    ELSE

Reverses the current IF branch. Use between IF and its matching FI. An
outer false condition continues to suppress nested commands.

Example: IF NULL X;ECHO SKIPPED;ELSE;ECHO SHOWN;FI

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
